 ## Background
-ContraNeRF was proposed by Hao Yang, Lanqing Hong, Aoxue Li, Tianyang Hu, Zhenguo Li, Gim Hee Lee, and Liwei Wang [S1]. It was published in CVPR 2023 (arXiv:2303.11052v3, 23 Jun 2023) [S1]. The work addresses the problem that vanilla NeRF is designed to fit the continuous 5D radiance field of a given scene and often fails to generalize to new scenes and datasets [S1]. It specifically tackles the synthetic-to-real generalization problem, where models trained on synthetic data exhibit specific artifacts related to volume density prediction [S1].
+ContraNeRF was proposed by Hao Yang, Lanqing Hong, Aoxue Li, Tianyang Hu, Zhenguo Li, Gim Hee Lee, and Liwei Wang [S1]. It was published in CVPR 2023 (arXiv:2303.11052v3, 23 Jun 2023) [S1]. The work addresses the limitations of vanilla NeRF, which is designed to fit the continuous 5D radiance field of a given scene and often fails to generalize to new scenes and datasets [S1]. It specifically tackles the issue that using synthetic data for training can lead to sharper but less accurate volume densities, causing artifacts in real-world scenarios [S1].
 
